{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban the sale of rabbits as domestic pets",
        "additional_details": "Rabbits can be classified as exotic pets due to their specialised care needs and unique physiology and need to be looked after correctly. They are bought mainly for children and then they can get neglected as the novelty wears off. Pet shops often sell hutches not fit for purpose, and rabbits can often be kept in them 24/7. We believe there are far too many rabbits needing to be re-homed because people realise they are not easy or cheap to care for properly.",
        "background": "We want the Government to ban the sale of rabbits as domestic pets. We feel that too many rabbits are neglected, kept in unsuitable hutches, and abandoned.",
